Apply the conditional exceptions before choosing loss IDs. An extra URL merely
referencing the same already stated license, with no new visible condition, is
not a loss: leave its side's loss ID empty. A literal missing pointer does not
override this rule. New license restrictions or obligations do require loss IDs.
Likewise, a currency label alone in an empty zero-value cart is not a loss.
A city/destination label alone is also not a loss when the rest of the complete
service description, stated procedure, actual price/rate and conditions match.
